      ],
      "defect": "An external reference — DNS CNAME, CDN origin, package- manager install URL, application configuration — points at an S3 bucket that does not exist in AWS or is not owned by the referencing account. The bucket name is unclaimed; anyone can register it with `aws s3api create-bucket`.\n",
      "infection": "An attacker claims the unclaimed bucket name and serves arbitrary content from it. Any downstream consumer following the reference — browsers resolving the CNAME, CDNs proxying the origin, package managers fetching install scripts — retrieves attacker content under a trusted-looking URL. Because the bucket's DNS and path appear legitimate (matching the original infrastructure), endpoint detection and user intuition both fail: the attacker's certificate validates, the hostname is familiar, the URL looks routine. Software-distribution takeover is the worst case: `curl | sh` style install commands execute attacker code.\n",
      "failure": "Attacker-controlled content delivery under a trusted identity. Remediation is complex because affected downstream consumers may have cached or installed attacker-delivered artifacts during the exposure window; full recovery requires re-verifying installed software, rotating credentials potentially captured, and invalidating cached content across CDNs and browser caches.\n",
      "delta": [
        {
          "property_label": "bucket exists",
          "property_path": "s3_ref.bucket_exists",
          "current_value": "false",
          "fix_action": "set to true (enable)"
        },
        {
          "property_label": "bucket owned",
          "property_path": "s3_ref.bucket_owned",
          "current_value": "false",
          "fix_action": "set to true (enable)"
        }
      ],
